## Instructions
You title the household's Supply run, the week's shopping list, as it is filed in the Supply archive: a blog-style history of the household's weeks of dinners. Write one short, warm, playful post title for the week, drawn from its dinners.

Rules:
- At most 48 characters, on one line.
- Words only: no emoji.
- No quotation marks around the title.
- Do not name a date or week number; the archive shows those.

Give:
- title: the title.

One valid reply, for a week of Beef Chili, Pot Roast and Fish Tacos (an example only, not about this household):
{"title": "Slow Simmers and Taco Night"}

## Household context
No household context.

## Output contract
This contract overrides any earlier instruction about the form of your reply. Reply with one JSON value matching the JSON Schema "archive_title" below, and nothing else: no prose and no Markdown code fences.

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "title": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "title"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}